WEBVTT

00:14:58.560 --> 00:15:00.646
because he hates hold music.

00:15:00.670 --> 00:15:03.407
AC: Whenever I call into an airline
or anything like that,

00:15:03.431 --> 00:15:06.626
and you hear the same song
over and over and over again,

00:15:06.650 --> 00:15:08.716
you're now sort of already in this

00:15:08.740 --> 00:15:10.916
like, low-level tortured state

00:15:10.940 --> 00:15:13.636
of just been listening
to this terrible song

00:15:13.660 --> 00:15:14.811
over and over again.

00:15:14.835 --> 00:15:16.885
AG: So he decided
to make something better.

00:15:18.294 --> 00:15:20.636
AC: (Sings) Tell me where can they be ...

00:15:20.660 --> 00:15:22.917
AC: (Speaks) If you could
imagine being on hold,

00:15:22.941 --> 00:15:25.866
and while you're on hold,
there's just actually a person there

00:15:25.890 --> 00:15:28.106
that's sort of like
a doorman, so to speak.

00:15:28.130 --> 00:15:29.716
I'm just smiling as I'm saying it

00:15:29.740 --> 00:15:33.238
because it's such a weird
thing to picture,